{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame","id":1157960,"title":"Development Board: Classic WoD Videogame","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-12T10:46:34-08:00","id":1157960,"title":"Development Board: Classic WoD Videogame","content":"So, we are going to try and create our own WoD videogame. This isn't going to be quick or easy, but if enough people want it done, it will be done.<br /> <br /> To this end, I'll alter this one post as regularly as possible to keep things updated in the front page.<br /> <br /> Contact with Paradox and White Wolf was already initiated. If we get a solid enough project, we can negotiate the licence.<br /> <br /> For now our workforce is:<br /> Game Director - Monteparnas<br /> Sound Director - Nail Eater<br /> <br /> I think this is right, but we need more. Any volunteers are welcome. The people giving ideas will be counted in, but this list is for specialty roles, so to speak.<br /> <br /> We can already start the brainstorm of ideas for the game. Lines, styles, mechanics. Until we have programmers we can't say for sure what will be feasible, but we can gather ideas. So, what kind of game do you want?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 11-21-2017, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T10:57:00-08:00","id":1157963,"title":"","content":"Do you have anything other than an idea? Can you program, write, or do art assets? And who is we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:49:00-08:00","id":1158036,"title":"","content":"Ok, count me in. I can give support for the story, add some NPCs (including a rock band of Garou with some lyrics as I said earlier). If my brother find some time he could wrote music for those lyrics so if we find a band we could record a few songs for the game (maybe my friend could help). And if I renew contact with my other friend (and if he still works for them) he could be our contact in EA Games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T03:59:04-08:00","id":1158123,"title":"","content":"As long as it does not use that awful metaplot from Revised, I am all for this endeavor! (Revised did have good mechanics though)<br /> <br /> I doubt this will go very far, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd set the game in early 1990's Chicago and use the First Edition Vampire: The Masquerade corebook and the original Chicago by Night as reference.<br /> <br /> A Chicago By Night video game would be freakin' awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 11-13-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T04:46:30-08:00","id":1158133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158123#post1158123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as it does not use that awful metaplot from Revised, I am all for this endeavor! (Revised did have good mechanics though)<br /> <br /> I doubt this will go very far, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd set the game in early 1990's Chicago and use the First Edition Vampire: The Masquerade corebook and the original Chicago by Night as reference.<br /> <br /> A Chicago By Night video game would be freakin' awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO revised metaplot wasn't entirely bad. I think that &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon&quot; was worse. And thank you for your wraith. I personally appreciate it. As for setting the problem is that there was no City book/rage across which describes entire population, Kindred, Garou, Mages etc. The closest were CbN, LAbN, RANY and NYbN. But do we have to use official books? Can't we create some kind of city book that would describe all supernatural population? We could even create our own city, just like St. Claire in Project Twilight, Tierburg in Dark Tower adventure or Ashcroft in Hunter video games. Heck, the French officially published a book that describe their country. Why can't we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:22:33-08:00","id":1158174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158133#post1158133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO revised metaplot wasn't entirely bad. I think that &quot;Under a Blood Red Moon&quot; was worse. And thank you for your wraith. I personally appreciate it. As for setting the problem is that there was no City book/rage across which describes entire population, Kindred, Garou, Mages etc. The closest were CbN, LAbN, RANY and NYbN. But do we have to use official books? Can't we create some kind of city book that would describe all supernatural population? We could even create our own city, just like St. Claire in Project Twilight, Tierburg in Dark Tower adventure or Ashcroft in Hunter video games. Heck, the French officially published a book that describe their country. Why can't we?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As long as the Gangrel are in the Camarilla and the Ravnos are a full clan, I'll play this. If you need help coming up with a fictional city, I can help you with that.<br /> <br /> The Week of Nightmares and Independent Gangrel are deal-breakers for me in terms of metaplot. I won't play any WoD game that recognizes those two metaplot points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T19:17:06-08:00","id":1158319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158123#post1158123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as it does not use that awful metaplot from Revised, I am all for this endeavor! (Revised did have good mechanics though)<br /> <br /> I doubt this will go very far, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd set the game in early 1990's Chicago and use the First Edition Vampire: The Masquerade corebook and the original Chicago by Night as reference.<br /> <br /> A Chicago By Night video game would be freakin' awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably we'll have some games that stay in the 1st Ed (lack of) metaplot, some that acknowledges Revised, and some that go nuts in our own metaplot. To achieve any collective endeavor, we need to be open to compromise, specially since we need the license, and so to accept the terms of White Wolf.<br /> <br /> Anyway, be welcome to comment and give ideas.<br /> <br /> For now we have a director for the project (me, until we decide not, but we need a start), and a music director. A good start, but we need someone with a minimal knowledge of the actual coding to give us ideas on what can be done, even if just as consultants. I know some people that maybe can help. I'll find out tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1157963#post1157963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have anything other than an idea? Can you program, write, or do art assets? And who is we?</div> </div> </div> </div>We is anyone in this forums that want to contribute. And I know something of management, accounting and other stuff that you need at the core of a project. I also have my experience working at a bank. We'll see if I can help, I'm not saying it is a sure thing, just that we can try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T22:46:46-08:00","id":1158364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame#post1157960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we are going to try and create our own WoD videogame. This isn't going to be quick or easy, but if enough people want it done, it will be done.<br /> <br /> To this end, I'll alter this one post as regularly as possible to keep things updated in the front page.<br /> <br /> First of all we need workforce. This thread can be used to discuss things with all the forum community, but we need some actual roles filled. People who want to contribute and have any kind of specialized abilities that could help, please state it here to be added to the staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which of the World of Darkness games - and which parts of them - would you say would be best to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T23:40:30-08:00","id":1158375,"title":"","content":"I have to cock my head at this, as what you're basically saying is... &quot;I have an idea! Would someone else like to make it for me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, how do you intend to avoid the copyright situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T00:43:20-08:00","id":1158387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158375#post1158375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to cock my head at this, as what you're basically saying is... &quot;I have an idea! Would someone else like to make it for me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't inherently bad, as often enough a person with the incentive to start and organize something is necessary for something to happen in the first place, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how do you intend to avoid the copyright situation? </div> </div> </div>This. Seriously guys. The first thing you might want to do is not gather people, but find out if WW would even let it fly. Else you get people excited, organized, perhaps even work put in, just to see it all torn down because you ignored that it isn't your IP. Right now you're already talking 'games' in plural before even doing this, for crissakes.<br /> <br /> Contact WW. Check with them. THEN, and only then if you get any kind of green light, even if it is just <i>'If the game is purely fan-made non-profit, we are okay with it.</i>' you should continue doing what you're doing here. Anything else before that is getting worked up towards disappointment.<br /> <br /> With WW's plans of wanting to get the WoD into all media, this is either the best time (i.e. them wanting to even let Fans make videogames) or the worst time (I.e. them really wanting to focus on polished, professional games first and foremost as an initial representation) to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-14-2017, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T16:14:18-08:00","id":1158691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158364#post1158364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the World of Darkness games - and which parts of them - would you say would be best to use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the matter we will discuss here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T16:24:46-08:00","id":1158696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158387#post1158387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Seriously guys. The first thing you might want to do is not gather people, but find out if WW would even let it fly. Else you get people excited, organized, perhaps even work put in, just to see it all torn down because you ignored that it isn't your IP. Right now you're already talking 'games' in plural before even doing this, for crissakes.<br /> <br /> Contact WW. Check with them. THEN, and only then if you get any kind of green light, even if it is just <i>'If the game is purely fan-made non-profit, we are okay with it.</i>' you should continue doing what you're doing here. Anything else before that is getting worked up towards disappointment.<br /> <br /> With WW's plans of wanting to get the WoD into all media, this is either the best time (i.e. them wanting to even let Fans make videogames) or the worst time (I.e. them really wanting to focus on polished, professional games first and foremost as an initial representation) to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're wrong. For now it's just an idea. First of all we have to decide what do we want: vampire, werewolf, mage or anything else. If someone come to me and way that he would like to use a world that I've created but don't know which part I surely will send him to hell and tell to meet me again when he will make a decision. Or have him pay for the licence for entire world no matter how much he will finally use. So I think that deciding what we want and check if we have the resources and manpower to do that then ask WW for permission is the proper order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-14-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:53:25-08:00","id":1158804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158696#post1158696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're wrong. For now it's just an idea. First of all we have to decide what do we want: vampire, werewolf, mage or anything else. If someone come to me and way that he would like to use a world that I've created but don't know which part I surely will send him to hell and tell to meet me again when he will make a decision. Or have him pay for the licence for entire world no matter how much he will finally use. So I think that deciding what we want and check if we have the resources and manpower to do that then ask WW for permission is the proper order.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm saying is, ASK THAT. Early. ASAP. Ask them <i>&quot;Hey WW. We're a bunch of diehard cWoD fans with years (decades) of experience, and we really, really want to make a nice &lt;gametype&gt;-style cWoD game. If we delivered you a well fleshed out, structured concept for a game, along with a neat prototype to show off what we have in mind and can do, would you be willing to take a look and give us a chance?&quot;</i><br /> The sooner you know the answer to that basic question, the better.<br /> <br /> Don't go in there with the work already done just for them to go <i>&quot;Oh, hi. No, sorry, Paradox has licensed companies X Y the exclusive rights to make those for now. Sorry. You're too late.&quot;</i> Or something along those lines. Because contracts like that are a thing, and not even the neatest presented work could change the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T10:37:44-08:00","id":1159479,"title":"","content":"It's funny. This topic was created for those who want to try. Up to now I see here many people with advises how to do it but none willing to contribute the skills to make it happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />t. As for licence: we have World of Darkness, Pent.... oooups, I almost said that, I meant Black Dog Game Factory of course released World of Twilight. Let's call it Evening Earth and problem solved :P.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:57:35-08:00","id":1159552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1159479#post1159479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Twilight</div> </div> </div> </div>Supermatural Flaw (10 Points)<br /> You sparkle. All the time.<br /> Any splat can take this.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for skills to make it happen, I have programming experience, I have strong interest in fanmade WoD games, and I really hope this succeeds if properly prepared...but sadly simply lack the RL time between work and other projects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So advice is all I can give!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:03:46-08:00","id":1159578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1159552#post1159552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supermatural Flaw (10 Points)<br /> You sparkle. All the time.<br /> Any splat can take this.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for skills to make it happen, I have programming experience, I have strong interest in fanmade WoD games, and I really hope this succeeds if properly prepared...but sadly simply lack the RL time between work and other projects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So advice is all I can give!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha. And if your name is Edward it becomes a merit.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of priorities. We still are discussing strategy and general ideas. Maybe in the future you'll find some time and join us.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T09:50:55-08:00","id":1160237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158364#post1158364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the World of Darkness games - and which parts of them - would you say would be best to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it is kept narrow enough to work as a video-game, anything can do. The main thing is to keep each game idea as just a facet of the setting, avoiding the urge to try to bring the entire tabletop experience to the game. A single story, self-contained, is enough to make a video-game. If more can be told, then more games can be created, there is no need to put too much in a single project.<br /> <br /> That said, each line can make for a couple of good starts. I'll try to give two initial ideas for each line I know well enough:<br /> <br /> Vampire - A game based on politics and management. There are some of those on the internet, and it could present an Ancillae getting its own little Domain to rule, dealing with rivals and rogue Kindred, and eventually with outsmarting old Elders at late game. Other option would be a psychological horror game like Silent Hill, with the twist of emphasis on your own Beast.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - I'm a fan of platformers, so it could be interesting to have something Metroidvanya style, with exploration of several locations to accomplish missions, maybe with not-so-allied factions like the Tribes being a relevant choices. Another option to avoid the too-obvious action carnage could be Strategy, with the player planing the action at the Caern to accomplish missions, manage other Packs, and maybe the option to go for Action by going with your own Pack.<br /> <br /> Mage - FPS was already proposed, and can be an interesting choice. It creates a narrow enough context for the Magic system to be implemented without getting out of hand. The Ascension is still a war, and several factions can go for several mission on it, with a fair share of allies and enemies of occasion. Alternately, an Exploration game could focus on a character's personal journey to Ascension, taking place during the Seeks, only. Most decisions can be let to happen during &quot;downtime&quot;, while the Seek teaches more about the truths of reality. With this approach, the character would be restricted as most Mages should be in the beginning, not knowing the true rules to which Magic answer.<br /> <br /> Changeling - Just occurred to me a Tactical Espionage Action in the likes of Metal Gear, with the common enemies being Banal people completely unaware of the true action occurring, mistaking you for a troublemaker and causing all the problems they can with their Banality around you. Other approach would be a light novel or other Decision-Oriented game for you to navigate the tragic path of choosing between Humanity and Dream, and ultimately between Forgetfulness and Madness.<br /> <br /> Demon - I can think of an investigative game to root out secrets from the War, and eventually to seek out and win over an Earthbound. The key to it could be time, measured directly or turn-like, as it could change the scenario in several ways. Other option could be a gathering game about faith similar to Star Control 2 The Ur-Quan Masters, with dynamic changes in the map.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158387#post1158387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't inherently bad, as often enough a person with the incentive to start and organize something is necessary for something to happen in the first place, but...<br /> <br /> This. Seriously guys. The first thing you might want to do is not gather people, but find out if WW would even let it fly. Else you get people excited, organized, perhaps even work put in, just to see it all torn down because you ignored that it isn't your IP. Right now you're already talking 'games' in plural before even doing this, for crissakes.<br /> <br /> Contact WW. Check with them. THEN, and only then if you get any kind of green light, even if it is just <i>'If the game is purely fan-made non-profit, we are okay with it.</i>' you should continue doing what you're doing here. Anything else before that is getting worked up towards disappointment.<br /> <br /> With WW's plans of wanting to get the WoD into all media, this is either the best time (i.e. them wanting to even let Fans make videogames) or the worst time (I.e. them really wanting to focus on polished, professional games first and foremost as an initial representation) to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that. I am already looking out for ways to contact them, and preparing for take into account Copyright expenses. My top priority right now, by the way, isn't programmers, but people who have contacts or experience with negotiation. I'll do some of this myself, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1158696#post1158696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're wrong. For now it's just an idea. First of all we have to decide what do we want: vampire, werewolf, mage or anything else. If someone come to me and way that he would like to use a world that I've created but don't know which part I surely will send him to hell and tell to meet me again when he will make a decision. Or have him pay for the licence for entire world no matter how much he will finally use. So I think that deciding what we want and check if we have the resources and manpower to do that then ask WW for permission is the proper order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this. Copyright negotiations tend to start with the first draft of a project. The first thing most companies will want to see is a clear picture of what you're planning to do with their licence. The most likely answer for asking with empty hands is that they'll hear us when we have something to show them.<br /> <br /> Either way, projects like this are ripe with unexpected turns and risks. Changing things to account for such an issue is a thing, as sad as it may be. A lot of similar projects went such a path, and not all of them are bad in the end. In worst case scenario for the copyright problem, our first game will be a rip-off, but will also work as something to increase our chances next time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1159552#post1159552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supermatural Flaw (10 Points)<br /> As for skills to make it happen, I have programming experience, I have strong interest in fanmade WoD games, and I really hope this succeeds if properly prepared...but sadly simply lack the RL time between work and other projects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So advice is all I can give!</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be welcome to give it, and to come on board with more if you find the time to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T06:31:35-08:00","id":1160497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160237#post1160237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage - FPS was already proposed, and can be an interesting choice. It creates a narrow enough context for the Magic system to be implemented without getting out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you think that designing and creating a Metroidvania-like game would be much more appropriate in regards to getting across the mood and the possibilities that are present in M:tA ; rather than an FPS game? For example, using True Magick to acess overcome obstacles and challenges, and access new areas in many different ways, could be designed to be very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T07:50:09-08:00","id":1160508,"title":"","content":"I've also have another idea to convince WW that we're able to do that. It could also be used by p&amp;p players and storytellers as some kind of feelies (like in old C64 or ZX Spectrum video games). Hell, I must admit that even I would be happy using it. But we need someone able to create some kind of random number generator for PC/Android/iOS. And it would also need some research to find enough companies (form every setting, from Vampire to Demon, not only Pentex based) to make it interesting. As a fan of business simulation games I was thinking about stock simulator for WoD. It could be a simple random number generator (I can be wrong, I'm not a programmer) which will generate share value for each company ever used in WoD setting few times a day or whenever the ST click the appropriate button. It could also include some kind of editor to put data about player character's company. Or it could be a simple game (something like Wall Street Kid) in which you try to make a fortune on Wall Street. This would be tougher because it should take into consideration main events like Robert Allred death or Monkeywrenches actions. But IMHO it would show WW that we are willing to do something and that we're able to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-19-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:05:22-08:00","id":1160661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160497#post1160497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you think that designing and creating a Metroidvania-like game would be much more appropriate in regards to getting across the mood and the possibilities that are present in M:tA ; rather than an FPS game? For example, using True Magick to acess overcome obstacles and challenges, and access new areas in many different ways, could be designed to be very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is a special conundrum because of the broad system. I do think you're right, but maybe it is too much for a first try. With the magic of Mage being too broad, the FPS narrows the purpose of the things being done, so there is space to broaden options and mechanics inside this limited function.<br /> <br /> But I could be overthinking it, I'm aware of that. I actually focused just on presenting 2 distinct ideas for each splat, so I avoided repeating myself. There is nothing we can't thought to add to the pool of ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T03:03:13-08:00","id":1160792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160661#post1160661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is a special conundrum because of the broad system. I do think you're right, but maybe it is too much for a first try. With the magic of Mage being too broad, the FPS narrows the purpose of the things being done, so there is space to broaden options and mechanics inside this limited function.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of an FPS do you think a Mt:A PC game would be? Which FPS PC game (or which FPS series) would be the one with which a designer could try to look at it's design, and use it for a Mt:A FPS PC game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:34:55-08:00","id":1160941,"title":"","content":"Make sure you're good to go with this in terms of copyright issues before you get started. Several friends of mine and I were thinking of working on an Exalted visual novel. Before we started though we contacted OPP but were told we would need to speak with CCP. It took almost two months to get a response from them and they said they weren't interested in allowing someone to use Exalted material in a video game, even if we offered it free to play or even just gave it to them to distribute, and that they would defend their copyright claim to the fullest. Now the old White Wolf copyrights are owned by Paradox. There's no telling what they'll say, but definitely make sure they're okay with it before you get started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:02:50-08:00","id":1160976,"title":"","content":"I just went on and asked them by e-mail. I got an answer from them this very morning.<br /> <br /> They gave me a document about the process for pitching to use their IP. It pretty much went from their treasure to their main product, though one they'll sell with extra care. Can't blame them.<br /> <br /> Basically, they want things on track. We do need to start work first, and contact them when we have a rounded project. We don't need to give a teaser of the game or such, but at least enough of a project to show that it is likely to be released. They want it to add to their IP, so maybe we will have to compromise a little, but that was expected. Metaplot will be sacred at least to begin with.<br /> <br /> Since we are not a well developed company, a teaser can actually be a good idea, but a solid project can do the trick. An actual company isn't a requirement, but can be a good idea on the road. In the end, they are open to discuss, but we do need to show something before talking business.<br /> <br /> We need some programmers, and at least an artist for visual concept. If anyone knows what else we may need, please add. Anything we don't get here will have to be obtained elsewhere. I'm already on track of the artist and a programmer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:44:48-08:00","id":1160989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160941#post1160941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sure you're good to go with this in terms of copyright issues before you get started. Several friends of mine and I were thinking of working on an Exalted visual novel. Before we started though we contacted OPP but were told we would need to speak with CCP. It took almost two months to get a response from them and they said they weren't interested in allowing someone to use Exalted material in a video game, even if we offered it free to play or even just gave it to them to distribute, and that they would defend their copyright claim to the fullest. Now the old White Wolf copyrights are owned by Paradox. There's no telling what they'll say, but definitely make sure they're okay with it before you get started.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've read about a guy who tried to rebuild Heart of Gaia from scraps. When WW found out about this project they told him to stop. So they were very protective about their copyright. On the other hand Monteparnas just got the answer from Paradox, so I think that's worth a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:47:49-08:00","id":1160991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160976#post1160976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just went on and asked them by e-mail. I got an answer from them this very morning.<br /> <br /> They gave me a document about the process for pitching to use their IP. It pretty much went from their treasure to their main product, though one they'll sell with extra care. Can't blame them.<br /> <br /> Basically, they want things on track. We do need to start work first, and contact them when we have a rounded project. We don't need to give a teaser of the game or such, but at least enough of a project to show that it is likely to be released. They want it to add to their IP, so maybe we will have to compromise a little, but that was expected. Metaplot will be sacred at least to begin with.<br /> <br /> Since we are not a well developed company, a teaser can actually be a good idea, but a solid project can do the trick. An actual company isn't a requirement, but can be a good idea on the road. In the end, they are open to discuss, but we do need to show something before talking business.<br /> <br /> We need some programmers, and at least an artist for visual concept. If anyone knows what else we may need, please add. Anything we don't get here will have to be obtained elsewhere. I'm already on track of the artist and a programmer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just as we said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I must confess that I was trying to &quot;sell&quot; them some ideas of mine to their W:tA game but I didn't got any answer. So I will post them here, but not today (lack of time in work).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-20-2017, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T02:59:42-08:00","id":1161114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1160976#post1160976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just went on and asked them by e-mail. I got an answer from them this very morning.<br /> <br /> They gave me a document about the process for pitching to use their IP. It pretty much went from their treasure to their main product, though one they'll sell with extra care. Can't blame them.<br /> <br /> Basically, they want things on track. We do need to start work first, and contact them when we have a rounded project. We don't need to give a teaser of the game or such, but at least enough of a project to show that it is likely to be released. They want it to add to their IP, so maybe we will have to compromise a little, but that was expected. Metaplot will be sacred at least to begin with.<br /> <br /> Since we are not a well developed company, a teaser can actually be a good idea, but a solid project can do the trick. An actual company isn't a requirement, but can be a good idea on the road. In the end, they are open to discuss, but we do need to show something before talking business.<br /> <br /> We need some programmers, and at least an artist for visual concept. If anyone knows what else we may need, please add. Anything we don't get here will have to be obtained elsewhere. I'm already on track of the artist and a programmer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the Paradox worker mention in the e-mail sent to you which of the games (as in: whether M:tA or W:tA or V:tM) they would prefer to be used in regards to the first PC game being designed, made and sold in shops?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T06:18:24-08:00","id":1161143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161114#post1161114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Paradox worker mention in the e-mail sent to you which of the games (as in: whether M:tA or W:tA or V:tM) they would prefer to be used in regards to the first PC game being designed, made and sold in shops?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they actually asked this. So as much as we probably have to make some compromise, it isn't that huge. They're not seeking producers, they're waiting for opportunities. That is pretty much how those things work when you turn IP into business. Old WW wasn't doing that.<br /> <br /> I'll update the OP, and start the ideas gathering. It is the best we can do for now, until we have enough of a development team to go a little further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T06:30:11-08:00","id":1161146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161143#post1161143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they actually asked this. So as much as we probably have to make some compromise, it isn't that huge. They're not seeking producers, they're waiting for opportunities. That is pretty much how those things work when you turn IP into business. Old WW wasn't doing that.<br /> <br /> I'll update the OP, and start the ideas gathering. It is the best we can do for now, until we have enough of a development team to go a little further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which of the WoD game lines do you think would be the best to set the first PC game in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T06:43:00-08:00","id":1161151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161146#post1161146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the WoD game lines do you think would be the best to set the first PC game in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want ideas on this, but personally I think a mobile game could be a better start. As clich\u00e9 as it is, Vampire always sells well, but Demon could make for an interesting alternative.<br /> <br /> This is only my first thoughts on it, though. We have several possibilities, including the ones I didn't thought of yet.<br /> <br /> Oh, the OP is updated, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T08:46:45-08:00","id":1161173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161151#post1161151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want ideas on this, but personally I think a mobile game could be a better start. As clich\u00e9 as it is, Vampire always sells well, but Demon could make for an interesting alternative.<br /> <br /> This is only my first thoughts on it, though. We have several possibilities, including the ones I didn't thought of yet.<br /> <br /> Oh, the OP is updated, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so do you want me to gather my ideas and post them here again or do you get them from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...wod-video-game</a> ? And could you explain to me what IP and OP means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-21-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:15:33-08:00","id":1161275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161173#post1161173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, so do you want me to gather my ideas and post them here again or do you get them from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...wod-video-game</a> ? And could you explain to me what IP and OP means?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is better to gather it all here, so everyone can see it in one place. It will be easier for all during the brainstorm.<br /> <br /> OP stands for either &quot;Opening Post&quot; or &quot;Opening Poster&quot;. The second means me, the first means the beginning of the thread. IP stands for Intelectual Property, it means both the setting and all its copyrighted aspects.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll get some programmers by here, and an artist specialized in CG. Probably I'll have something to say about this on Monday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:36:18-08:00","id":1161349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161275#post1161275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is better to gather it all here, so everyone can see it in one place. It will be easier for all during the brainstorm.<br /> <br /> OP stands for either &quot;Opening Post&quot; or &quot;Opening Poster&quot;. The second means me, the first means the beginning of the thread. IP stands for Intelectual Property, it means both the setting and all its copyrighted aspects.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll get some programmers by here, and an artist specialized in CG. Probably I'll have something to say about this on Monday.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so here are my ideas:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Jungle War - a strategy game resembling Star Wars Rebellion. The story: Golgol Fangs First is dead. You are his succesor. You have to win the Amazon War. You have to send the packs to fight, send recruiters to the other septs to gain support for your efforts. And also battles could be implemented into the game, either RTS style, like in Total War series or tactical, like in Jagged Alliance.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Red Carpet Fighting Club - inspired by Giovanni Chronicles part IV. A fighting game. Choose a fighter or create your own (standard today) and win the illegal tournament organized by Giovanni clan mobsters. Optional there could be bribery to ease the game or betting (like in The Con video game). And roaring 20's jazz in the background. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">EWW - wrestling video game inspired by Children of the Night book. Choose or create a wrestler (mortal or supernatural) and become the champion in Pentex owned wrestling federation. Also it could include managerial options. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Corporate Wolf - inspired by events from my games. Business simulation game. The plot: finally Glass Walkers convinced other tribes that to defeat the Wyrm is to tackle Pentex. You are Michael Donelly, a Glass Walker Philodox investor to which entire garou nation money was given. Your goal: eliminate every Pentex company one by one. Choose your path by dominating the global market.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prince of the City - inspired by Sim City and The Sims. Simulation of a Camarilla Prince. I've read once about Simsville, a game never released but resembling this concept.<br /> The Rack - a nightclub management game. You are the owner of nightclub which is an Elysium and you have to take care for it. This means maintaining the supply, the Masquerade and sometimes Lupines attack.<br /> A caern builder. You found an abandoned/destroyed caern and you have to to make it functional again. You have to choose the participants of the rite from incoming characters (like in HOM&amp;M) basing on their auspice and tribe to avoid conflicts (like in Jagged Alliance or Baldurs Gate), choose the best moment for a rite (so the caern could be effectively reopened; and there should be enough garou to perform the rite), defend it (RTT or turn based tactical game elements) and organise the sept to avoid conflicts (Sims like elements).<br /> An idea of a game resembling The Sims, for adults of course, for supernaturals (something like The Sims Nightlife). And the quests could be published as mods or DLCs. Of course it would also have multiplayer option, even if I don't like MMO because I saw too many people playing those games and not feeling the climate of those games. There could also be the possibility to export your characters to other WoD games (maybe using my other ideas) so you could be anyone (a businessman in Corporate Wolf, the commander in Jungle War).<br /> <br /> That's all for now. But I found some interesting concepts creators to by other, but I don't want to post them here because I don't want to &quot;steal&quot; someone's else ideas. I think, basing on number of games, that the easiest one to create would be Red Carpet Fighting Club and EWW, but I'd like to hear professional opinion of the programmer.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the explanation. I didn't know that.<br /> <br /> As for artists I still try to convince my girlfriend to help us by making concept arts (she has a master's degree from The Academy of Fine Arts in \u0141\u00f3d\u017a) but without any success <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I also try to reach my friend, a heavy metal singer, to convince him to help us. Today I will also speak with my brother and ask him if he will find time to compose music for our project. If not I'm concerning other options. As for sound edition I could do it myself (example of my abilities I could send privately).</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-22-2017, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T00:20:39-08:00","id":1161441,"title":"","content":"Fighting games are popular, but I heard they're far harder to program than it seems. I'm already in contact with a friend that work a little with this kind of game. He's mostly a hobbyist, but will know directions from there. I'll also contact another friend that have both an Art degree in the University of Bras\u00edlia, and another in IT. Last time I heard of it, he was interested in game creation, so he's my best shot for now.<br /> <br /> Lately I'm thinking a lot in the time mechanics of Star Control 2 Ur-Quan Masters. In it, there is an entire setting and several plots running themselves independently, with a huge amount of ways the player can intersect with such stories and affect them, plus the consequences of those distinct interactions playing themselves as those plots can also intersect one another. It is a length game that really makes you feel that your personal choices matter and have unforeseen effects.<br /> <br /> Plus, I like resources management and gathering, so I like your ideas, and SC2 is mostly a gathering game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T01:16:58-08:00","id":1161449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161151#post1161151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want ideas on this, but personally I think a mobile game could be a better start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think a PC game would be unviable in regards to being the first game made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T03:13:23-08:00","id":1161460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161441#post1161441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fighting games are popular, but I heard they're far harder to program than it seems. I'm already in contact with a friend that work a little with this kind of game. He's mostly a hobbyist, but will know directions from there. I'll also contact another friend that have both an Art degree in the University of Bras\u00edlia, and another in IT. Last time I heard of it, he was interested in game creation, so he's my best shot for now.<br /> <br /> Lately I'm thinking a lot in the time mechanics of Star Control 2 Ur-Quan Masters. In it, there is an entire setting and several plots running themselves independently, with a huge amount of ways the player can intersect with such stories and affect them, plus the consequences of those distinct interactions playing themselves as those plots can also intersect one another. It is a length game that really makes you feel that your personal choices matter and have unforeseen effects.<br /> <br /> Plus, I like resources management and gathering, so I like your ideas, and SC2 is mostly a gathering game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I was basing on popularity. I don't have any IT skills but I am good with audio processing programs. I also like management games (almost all of them, from Capitalism to sports managers) so if it would be easier we could start with them. As for fighting games IMHO it don't have to be like Street Fighter or Mortal Combat. Now I am editing data for my personal use in TEW 2005 to create EWW federation (from Children of the Night p. 72). It's a fighting/manager text based video game. The same solution was used in Wrestling Spirit. Maybe that's the way to make fighting game easier to create. What do you think about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T17:24:00-08:00","id":1161665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161449#post1161449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think a PC game would be unviable in regards to being the first game made?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. I just think a mobile game would be easier to develop, offer and sell. And I could be wrong on this. But mobile games are a trend because they're easily accessible to the buyer. Also, it lets us use the marketing formula of a free game with built-in purchases, and if done right it makes a game even more accessible. As an example, a Vampire-based game could have the seven Core Clans to start with, and new clans and bloodlines as paid DLCs at $1 each. Or even at 50 cents, I don't know, so things get a little cheaper in other countries.<br /> <br /> But this is just an idea being thrown on the basket. Nothing is out for now. First we gather a good amount of ideas, later we will select our first project and start the hard(er) work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161460#post1161460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I was basing on popularity. I don't have any IT skills but I am good with audio processing programs. I also like management games (almost all of them, from Capitalism to sports managers) so if it would be easier we could start with them. As for fighting games IMHO it don't have to be like Street Fighter or Mortal Combat. Now I am editing data for my personal use in TEW 2005 to create EWW federation (from Children of the Night p. 72). It's a fighting/manager text based video game. The same solution was used in Wrestling Spirit. Maybe that's the way to make fighting game easier to create. What do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't played such games, so I'm not familiar with it. I'll take a look, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T19:15:25-08:00","id":1161708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1161665#post1161665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't played such games, so I'm not familiar with it. I'll take a look, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am quite familiar with those games. They are very similar to p. ex. Championship Manager (older edition of Football Manager). No graphics except static background images, large players/staff/clubs database, no sound but cheering of the crowds, and you know how your team is playing by reading commentary. Choosing match tactics takes 2.5 h. average. Theoretically boring as hell. But CM series have almost cult status among soccer fans. Merits of fighting games created that way? They can be completed not by blindly pushing the buttons or learning combos but by strategy and proper use of maneuvers you've read about during the game. Main flaw of fighting games created that way? They can be completed not by blindly pushing the buttons or learning combos but by strategy and proper use of maneuvers you've read about during the game. I have an idea how to ballance mortal and supernatural characters in EWW game concept. Unfortunately my friend who usually filled my concepts with flesh and blood game mechanics died few years ago but I think it's can be done without him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-23-2017, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T03:38:16-08:00","id":1161811,"title":"","content":"Heck, I was inspired by my own post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Please ask your friend how difficult would be to create a game which is something similar to Football Manager or New Star Soccer 1 and 2 compared to NSS 3-5? Text based and fighting game simultaneously? You know, if you lack of reflex you can use text based version (something like CCG) and if you want you can play it like a normal fighting game using your reflexes and combos. Theoretically it could be done relatively easy. Anything you need to create a text based version is a bunch of fighters with stories and maneuvers and mechanics that will calculate the odds of winning and you have a complete game. And it will be a thing that can be shown to Paradox. A fighting game is another thing, as you said it's not as easy as it looks. But I think that we could create a text based version and if Paradox will be interested they could upgrade it to a fighting game version based on our fighters, genres etc. My other idea is of course some kind of strategy/management simulation game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:26:10-08:00","id":1162309,"title":"","content":"I've just got ourselves a Graphic Designer to start with. Better, his also a lawyer, so we'll have the law part covered, at least as a consultant (since we're not on USA, I don't know if he can represent us there, but it is a good start, anyway).<br /> <br /> My fighting-games &quot;specialist&quot; is coming to my house by now, so I'll soon ask about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T21:01:09-08:00","id":1162338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1162309#post1162309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just got ourselves a Graphic Designer to start with. Better, his also a lawyer, so we'll have the law part covered, at least as a consultant (since we're not on USA, I don't know if he can represent us there, but it is a good start, anyway).<br /> <br /> My fighting-games &quot;specialist&quot; is coming to my house by now, so I'll soon ask about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend is also a lawyer, here in Poland. I think that he could help us with EU law too. As for copyrights I would also try to hook up to Storyteller's Vault. If WW give people a chance to publish something with their blessing, even if it's rubbish, maybe we could do it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T13:17:32-08:00","id":1162537,"title":"","content":"Got a guy who have both a degree in arts and in video-games. Enough programmers already to evaluate the viability of each idea.<br /> <br /> So that's it. Lets continue to produce ideas. Develop on those freely for now. During the week I'll start to guide the process into something we can poll. I'm expecting to have around 5 well-rounded ideas in one or two weeks to give to the programming team evaluate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T14:35:36-08:00","id":1162555,"title":"","content":"OK. My ideas you already have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. But it seems that, during last few days we are the only active people here. I hope that there will be more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T14:53:21-08:00","id":1163343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1162555#post1162555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. My ideas you already have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. But it seems that, during last few days we are the only active people here. I hope that there will be more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll ask you to elaborate further on the previous ideas, both yours and mine. I was starting to do it last night, but my cat was beaten up to almost death and is in the veterinarian now, so I'm really not in the mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:24:56-08:00","id":1163559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1163343#post1163343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I'll ask you to elaborate further on the previous ideas, both yours and mine. I was starting to do it last night, but my cat was beaten up to almost death and is in the veterinarian now, so I'm really not in the mood.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Sorry to hear that. I hope that he (or she, I can't make myself to call animals it) will be all right. I can imagine how you feel. I'm a dog/rat person and I have to say final goodbye to two of the latter last 3 months. Do you know who could did it?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Anyway the ideas. As I said Jungle War resembles Star Wars Rebellion. I imagine 3 mods:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- You play as Golgol Fangs First. You have to send recruiters to the other septs to gain support for your cause. They could be more or less effective. Their effectiveness will bring you warriors and you have to group them into wargs judging by p. ex. their tribes. As we all know a pair Get of Fenris and Black Fury will be less effective than Get of Fenris and Fianna. And then you have to send them to battle with Pentex and sometimes with Balams like in normal strategy games.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- The Succesor is mostly the same but you are Golgol's succesor. And you have to prove yourself worth. So your recruiters will be less effective (if Golgol lost his life how your chances look like) and morale of your troops will be lower. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">-Career - you start as a Warg/pack leader and slowly you climb on the chain of command. First of all it is a turn based/real time tactical game (like in Jagged Alliance or SWAT respectively). You get sometimes new warriors, greenhorns and veterans alike (Golgol sends them to your unit). Ultimate goal: became Golgol's succesor (see above, but here you will be nominated by him so recruiters will have normal skills and your troops normal morale)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Of course you could also include mode that allows you to play as Pentex (less powers, better Technology but your troops are prone to go postal) or as Balams (weakest troops, but fastest movement - after all it's your jungle, tactical modifiers - and you know your yard very well, and don't forget Mokole as some kind of artillery). Of course you could also meet civilians, like Indians or archeologists, some vampires (there was mentioned about Setites and Gangrels in various books) maybe even some mages or mummies. And if you want we could also include all kinds of all other supernaturals).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Corporate Wolf - as I said purely management game like Capitalism. The plot: Glass Walkers convinced other tribes that to defeat the Wyrm is to tackle Pentex. They gave all their resources to you. And you have to take over Pentex by buying their stocks. You create your character (simple mechanics, like in Bloodlines, Charisma, Manipulation, Intelligence and Wits as stats, Bureaucracy, Computers, Expression, Investigation and Subterfuge as skills). As I let my players create a superheroes characters I would let the player create a character with max skills I've mentioned above. On the other hand one crisis could drown character like that thus ending the game. And now: Charisma and Expression are used to convince other Garou to give you some more money if you're in trouble. Manipulation and Subterfuge to convince independent ivestors (or Syndicate) to sell you their shares. Wits and Investigation or Computers to find some dirt on Pentex companies (thus lowering the price of shares) and Intelligence and Bureaucracy to predict the prices. Of course you have to deal with many competitors also (Syndicate, Ventrue, rich mortals). If you're succesful you could became a Pentex CEO (if we put there some kind of Dark/Light Side mechanics like in Jedi Knight you could be either a saviour or bringer of the Apocalypse in the end), if your judgement will be constantly wrong the tribes could end their support and take their money away (and that could hurt you more than bad investment)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Red Carpet Fighting Club - either a fighting game or sports manager. In fighting version you choose (or create) a fighter to compete in a Giovanni sponsored underground fighting tournament described in Giovanni Chronicles part IV Nuova Malattia. It could be either text based (like in first two parts of New Star Soccer, you get the description of your situations like the wall is 2 ft behind you, 5 ft on the right and 27 ft on the left. Your opponent is throwing a left hook on your Head. What do you do? And then you choose from some options like dodge, run on left/right/back/forward, punch, kick etc.) and the AI calculate your chances for succes basing on your and your opponents stats. Or it could be normal fighting game but like Pit Fighter coin up rather than Mortal Combat (Giovanni are not stupid so they won't allow other supernaturals to participate). As for sports management game you are a Giovanni vampire. You have some money into your pocket and you have to rent the arena (it could be everywhere, from trailer park to warehouse to nightclub) find some fighters, find some security (it is neccesary, this tournament is illegal so police raid could happen, not to mention the Prohibition and you sell booze there, right) and set ticket prices. And watch as your resources increases <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">EWW - wrestling video game, this time with supernaturals. Extreme Wrestling Warfare was mentioned in Children of the Night. You choose or create a wrestler (either supernatural or mortal, mortals don't have superpowers but more combat maneuvers and I think that the greatest mortal fighters are able to defeat even Garou in Crinos form) and fight in a hardcore tournament. I have some ideas for stipulations, p. ex. Live Wire where ropes are live wires not strong enough to kill but to seriously wound. In normal wrestling it could dissalowed saving one from counting by placing ones leg on the ropes. Mechanics like described above, either text based or normal fighting. It could be also stable manager. This time you are a pack leader who, with his packmates, wants to win the belt and then destroy entire federation. You set your strategy, choose the fighters and hope that they won't be killed (as I said it is a hard core wrestling federation, Wyrm version). Or it could be sports manager where you are the CEO of EWW and you have to find fighters, sponsors, negotiate contracts, evolve storylines etc. Just like in TEW video games.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And a caern builder (no title for now). Something between Sim City, Jagged Alliance and The Sims. You choose an abandoned caern (there are plenty of them described in various books). You have to complete the proper number of Garou (random generated, like in HOMAM) to open the caern (possible conflicts between tribes), defend the place from Wyrm, mages and all other competitors (tactical game). And, if you want, continue the game after the caern was opened as a sept leader (like in The Sims, possible conflicts as above).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">These are my ideas. Unfortunetaly my friend who was a genius with numbers and could help us with mechanics died 10 years ago so please ask your friends which one of those will be possible to create and let me know. I can help with my imagination creating NPCs and places and of course with music.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And best wishes for your cat. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-30-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:45:34-08:00","id":1164028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1163559#post1163559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:H