judgement will be constantly wrong the tribes could end their support and take their money away (and that could hurt you more than bad investment)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Red Carpet Fighting Club - either a fighting game or sports manager. In fighting version you choose (or create) a fighter to compete in a Giovanni sponsored underground fighting tournament described in Giovanni Chronicles part IV Nuova Malattia. It could be either text based (like in first two parts of New Star Soccer, you get the description of your situations like the wall is 2 ft behind you, 5 ft on the right and 27 ft on the left. Your opponent is throwing a left hook on your Head. What do you do? And then you choose from some options like dodge, run on left/right/back/forward, punch, kick etc.) and the AI calculate your chances for succes basing on your and your opponents stats. Or it could be normal fighting game but like Pit Fighter coin up rather than Mortal Combat (Giovanni are not stupid so they won't allow other supernaturals to participate). As for sports management game you are a Giovanni vampire. You have some money into your pocket and you have to rent the arena (it could be everywhere, from trailer park to warehouse to nightclub) find some fighters, find some security (it is neccesary, this tournament is illegal so police raid could happen, not to mention the Prohibition and you sell booze there, right) and set ticket prices. And watch as your resources increases <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">EWW - wrestling video game, this time with supernaturals. Extreme Wrestling Warfare was mentioned in Children of the Night. You choose or create a wrestler (either supernatural or mortal, mortals don't have superpowers but more combat maneuvers and I think that the greatest mortal fighters are able to defeat even Garou in Crinos form) and fight in a hardcore tournament. I have some ideas for stipulations, p. ex. Live Wire where ropes are live wires not strong enough to kill but to seriously wound. In normal wrestling it could dissalowed saving one from counting by placing ones leg on the ropes. Mechanics like described above, either text based or normal fighting. It could be also stable manager. This time you are a pack leader who, with his packmates, wants to win the belt and then destroy entire federation. You set your strategy, choose the fighters and hope that they won't be killed (as I said it is a hard core wrestling federation, Wyrm version). Or it could be sports manager where you are the CEO of EWW and you have to find fighters, sponsors, negotiate contracts, evolve storylines etc. Just like in TEW video games.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And a caern builder (no title for now). Something between Sim City, Jagged Alliance and The Sims. You choose an abandoned caern (there are plenty of them described in various books). You have to complete the proper number of Garou (random generated, like in HOMAM) to open the caern (possible conflicts between tribes), defend the place from Wyrm, mages and all other competitors (tactical game). And, if you want, continue the game after the caern was opened as a sept leader (like in The Sims, possible conflicts as above).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">These are my ideas. Unfortunetaly my friend who was a genius with numbers and could help us with mechanics died 10 years ago so please ask your friends which one of those will be possible to create and let me know. I can help with my imagination creating NPCs and places and of course with music.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And best wishes for your cat. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Just got news that my cat will live. Probably will be blind of an eye for good, and maybe won't eat solid thing anymore, but at least is out of danger and can come home tomorrow. I'll have about two or three months pretending that paper is food just to afford for his health, but I don't care.<br /> <br /> <b>Jungle Wars</b>:<br /> I like the idea of the Career. Also, you could have Representatives, groups you manage from afar to gather help from the world around, or that were sent by others to your army, and now you have to deal with &quot;not-quite-a-spy-but-kind-of&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> Balams could work for a more Tactical Action game with a single unit or very few of them, given how they usually work. Mokol\u00e9s can make for a very distinct game play, with Mnesis working as a source of advanced information, and deployment being a far more logistics-heavy decision, but each unit is an entirely distinct set of options by itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Corporate Wolf</b>:<br /> Could be expanded to Corporate Wars. Instead of just Garou trying to tackle Pentex, it could be each faction in the WoD that deals with the Corporate world trying to establish their power bases and accomplish their individual goals. For a casual game, you take a noob in the business world and vie for control of a city, or at least a city's aspect important for you. You don't necessarily need to actually wipe out others, but they can get in your way or help you by chasing their own goals. For an Ultimate Campaign, your final goal is as world shaking as the Apocalypse itself, from Garou accomplishing to force balance to the Wyrm (and maybe starting the Time of the Weaver), to Augustus Giovanni finally gathering the resources and knowledge needed to claim godhood.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Carpet Fighting Club</b>:<br /> What about a progression in the story mode, going from an all-human league to a Ghouled league? For the Fighting Game, it could open for the player to buy Disciplines, customizing the fighter, and other benefits from a Vampire sponsor. Also, we could add a Sponsor Mode, where instead of taking care of the entire league, you play one vampire that concentrates on bringing fighters. A character that pretty much needs a sheet similar to the one you though for Corporate Wolf, because it defines the means the character have to find, get, train and empower the fighters.<br /> <br /> <b>Caern Builder</b>:<br /> Adding other factions to this can be simpler than it seems while the focus stays on the general management. On some level, Caerns, Domains, Chantries and Free Holds work similarly. And they share the same World of Darkness. They could add another level of possible interactions, and the player be given free reign to decide on uncommon relationships, like allying with vampires or even with a specific sept of BSDs, to see what happens. I would add elements of The Settlers, because I love that game.<br /> <br /> For now I'll rest a little, but latter I'll add some of my own ideas. As soon as I can, I'll start to discuss all of this with the programmers to get the first feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T03:37:03-08:00","id":1164215,"title":"","content":"I was interested but am hesitant to jump in because of two reasons. One is time constraint and the other is the genre. IMHO since WoD is an RPG, then an RPG is the best fit.<br /> <br /> Allow me to voice my thought. At the bare minimum I suggest you have: a programmer and an animator. It seems you have a music (and sound) guy, that's nice.<br /> <br /> <b>Project Manager</b><br /> Ideally there should be a project manager. He decides the direction of project, create continuous detailed step-by-step progressions and whip everyone's butts to keep on track. Basically he's who everyone hates but needs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most hobbyist programmers lack the experience and skills to collaborate (and play nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) with others.<br /> <br /> <b>Programming</b><br /> It makes or breaks the project. Decide fast on platform, technology, testing methods and stick to them!<br /> <br /> Platform: Windows (XP+, 7+, 10+ so on), Macos, Linux, Xbox, Playstation, Andorid, Windows Mobile so on. The most widespread is of course Windows (version XP is no longer supported, 7 and above has the most share, 10 is up and coming but not too widespread yet). I recommend Windows 7 and above.<br /> <br /> Technology: simplest explanations is 2D or 3D. For a new team with minimum experience, go 2D. It simplifies a lot and still looks good. As a bonus, it has much lower system requirements which translate as wider audience.<br /> <br /> <b>How much is the budget? When is the deadline?</b> If you have money, to safe time and lots of pains, license some ready made engines. If minimum budget then the programmer needs to build some new engines from scratch. Which means lots of time, lots of bugs, lots of headache. If you have a programmer who is proficient in C++, then you're in luck. C# is okay for simple hobbyist projects and Java has sub par performance. Forget about other languages.<br /> <br /> <b>Animation</b><br /> Unless you're creating a text only game or have static graphics, you need an animator to create dynamic graphic (thus, more lifelike). How amazing do you want the graphic? Depends on the programming.<br /> <br /> <b>Audio</b><br /> Same as visual, depends on programming. Avoid voice/speech for first project. It requires more time and equipment, harder to change the lines, more i18n l10n works.<br /> <br /> <b>Testing / QA</b><br /> Most newcomers neglect this. But you really need a good QA. Can't stress this enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Documentation</b><br /> Prevent headache later on by paying attention on this from the very beginning. Maintain a good docs.<br /> <br /> WoD is a very complicated game. Thinking of translating just the core manual alone into code gives me a headache. So start small. Don't refer to professional games, especially those made by highly funded studios. Look at independent games made by small team.<br /> <br /> Maybe build a 10-hour RPG with a linear story with a few NPCs and one fixed PC. Trust me, even 10-hour gameplay is a lot of work for an RPG! (I'm talking about a good story-based RPG here not a button mashing action &quot;RPG&quot;.).<br /> <br /> If you do start this project, <b>persevere</b>! A project is always the most fun before it begins. It goes downhill fast and only becomes worse and worse. The grueling hard work, expenses, emotional distress, real life distractions, unreached expectations can all be too much too soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23565-azalae","name":"azalae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:43:36-08:00","id":1164424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was interested but am hesitant to jump in because of two reasons. One is time constraint and the other is the genre. IMHO since WoD is an RPG, then an RPG is the best fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>RPG is still as good a call as anything else. I just avoided it until now because most people would expect a precise and extensive translation from Pen &amp; Paper to Computer. Be welcome, anyway, everyone is welcome to take a part in the discussion of the project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to voice my thought. At the bare minimum I suggest you have: a programmer and an animator. It seems you have a music (and sound) guy, that's nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have more than one of each already, actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Project Manager</b><br /> Ideally there should be a project manager. He decides the direction of project, create continuous detailed step-by-step progressions and whip everyone's butts to keep on track. Basically he's who everyone hates but needs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most hobbyist programmers lack the experience and skills to collaborate (and play nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless someone else wants to take the job and everyone agrees, that is me. I have some experience coordinating unruly people, and I work with finances, I'm not used to be loved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Programming</b><br /> It makes or breaks the project. Decide fast on platform, technology, testing methods and stick to them!<br /> <br /> Platform: Windows (XP+, 7+, 10+ so on), Macos, Linux, Xbox, Playstation, Andorid, Windows Mobile so on. The most widespread is of course Windows (version XP is no longer supported, 7 and above has the most share, 10 is up and coming but not too widespread yet). I recommend Windows 7 and above.<br /> <br /> Technology: simplest explanations is 2D or 3D. For a new team with minimum experience, go 2D. It simplifies a lot and still looks good. As a bonus, it has much lower system requirements which translate as wider audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already scheduling a meeting with my team of programmers to discuss on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How much is the budget? When is the deadline?</b> If you have money, to safe time and lots of pains, license some ready made engines. If minimum budget then the programmer needs to build some new engines from scratch. Which means lots of time, lots of bugs, lots of headache. If you have a programmer who is proficient in C++, then you're in luck. C# is okay for simple hobbyist projects and Java has sub par performance. Forget about other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The budget is a tricky question, but one that's on my mind since before I started this thread. As I said, I work with money, literally. So I'm waiting for the first two or three meetings to define the project and define the means to form a budget.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Animation</b><br /> Unless you're creating a text only game or have static graphics, you need an animator to create dynamic graphic (thus, more lifelike). How amazing do you want the graphic? Depends on the programming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two, both professionals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Audio</b><br /> Same as visual, depends on programming. Avoid voice/speech for first project. It requires more time and equipment, harder to change the lines, more i18n l10n works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for now it isn't where I'm working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Testing / QA</b><br /> Most newcomers neglect this. But you really need a good QA. Can't stress this enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's a QA? Anyway, I'll take care with selecting testers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Documentation</b><br /> Prevent headache later on by paying attention on this from the very beginning. Maintain a good docs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Planning on this, already. I have some experience with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD is a very complicated game. Thinking of translating just the core manual alone into code gives me a headache. So start small. Don't refer to professional games, especially those made by highly funded studios. Look at independent games made by small team.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not planning on translate the actual rules at all. This is not how it works, and I know this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe build a 10-hour RPG with a linear story with a few NPCs and one fixed PC. Trust me, even 10-hour gameplay is a lot of work for an RPG! (I'm talking about a good story-based RPG here not a button mashing action &quot;RPG&quot;.).</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire idea includes limiting the scope of the game to keep things at a workable level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do start this project, <b>persevere</b>! A project is always the most fun before it begins. It goes downhill fast and only becomes worse and worse. The grueling hard work, expenses, emotional distress, real life distractions, unreached expectations can all be too much too soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I'm prepared to do this. My work is already incredibly boring and stressing, and yet I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:48:17-08:00","id":1164583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164028#post1164028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got news that my cat will live. Probably will be blind of an eye for good, and maybe won't eat solid thing anymore, but at least is out of danger and can come home tomorrow. I'll have about two or three months pretending that paper is food just to afford for his health, but I don't care.<br /> <br /> <b>Jungle Wars</b>:<br /> I like the idea of the Career. Also, you could have Representatives, groups you manage from afar to gather help from the world around, or that were sent by others to your army, and now you have to deal with &quot;not-quite-a-spy-but-kind-of&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> Balams could work for a more Tactical Action game with a single unit or very few of them, given how they usually work. Mokol\u00e9s can make for a very distinct game play, with Mnesis working as a source of advanced information, and deployment being a far more logistics-heavy decision, but each unit is an entirely distinct set of options by itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Corporate Wolf</b>:<br /> Could be expanded to Corporate Wars. Instead of just Garou trying to tackle Pentex, it could be each faction in the WoD that deals with the Corporate world trying to establish their power bases and accomplish their individual goals. For a casual game, you take a noob in the business world and vie for control of a city, or at least a city's aspect important for you. You don't necessarily need to actually wipe out others, but they can get in your way or help you by chasing their own goals. For an Ultimate Campaign, your final goal is as world shaking as the Apocalypse itself, from Garou accomplishing to force balance to the Wyrm (and maybe starting the Time of the Weaver), to Augustus Giovanni finally gathering the resources and knowledge needed to claim godhood.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Carpet Fighting Club</b>:<br /> What about a progression in the story mode, going from an all-human league to a Ghouled league? For the Fighting Game, it could open for the player to buy Disciplines, customizing the fighter, and other benefits from a Vampire sponsor. Also, we could add a Sponsor Mode, where instead of taking care of the entire league, you play one vampire that concentrates on bringing fighters. A character that pretty much needs a sheet similar to the one you though for Corporate Wolf, because it defines the means the character have to find, get, train and empower the fighters.<br /> <br /> <b>Caern Builder</b>:<br /> Adding other factions to this can be simpler than it seems while the focus stays on the general management. On some level, Caerns, Domains, Chantries and Free Holds work similarly. And they share the same World of Darkness. They could add another level of possible interactions, and the player be given free reign to decide on uncommon relationships, like allying with vampires or even with a specific sept of BSDs, to see what happens. I would add elements of The Settlers, because I love that game.<br /> <br /> For now I'll rest a little, but latter I'll add some of my own ideas. As soon as I can, I'll start to discuss all of this with the programmers to get the first feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear that your cat will be all right, at least quite all right. As for your upgrades:<br /> <br /> Jungle War - I've got nothing to are, like your ideas<br /> Corporate Wolf - I don't see the game which main goal is to control a part (or entire) city. I was thinking about a game resembling Capitalism not Gangsters. I didn't mention other fractions cause I thougt it is as clear as a day that they could (and should) be used. <br /> Red Carpet Fighting Club - I don't know if Sponsor Mode will be good. I was trying to create something cannon (taking the idea from Giovanni Chronicles part IV Nuova Malattia) so the vampire you talking about should be a Giovanni. I don't think that other clans would be allowed to participate. And I was also thinking about putting there some kind of superhero warriors (agents of Children of Isaac).<br /> Caern builder - the same as in Corporate Wolf. I had other fractions in kind, I just thought it isn't neccesary to mention them.<br /> <br /> My 2 new ideas<br /> Gaia's Dying Breath - You are Margrave Yuri Konietzko, the last of great Garou leaders and you have to lead others to the Last Battle. Grand strategy game.<br /> Tenebrae Bellum (I don't speak latin, just thought it sounds cool :P) - the year is 1940 and you are the commander of a secret Allied unit, consisted of various supernatural and lead a shadow war against supernaturals supporting the Nazis. Either a Commandos or Brigade e5 type game. More details next week, cause I will be off-line. I will also try to win my brother as a composer to our project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:52:51-08:00","id":1164586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azalae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame?p=1164215#post1164215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was interested but am hesitant to jump in because of two reasons. One is time constraint and the other is the genre. IMHO since WoD is an RPG, then an RPG is the best fit.<br /> <br /> Allow me to voice my thought. At the bare minimum I suggest you have: a programmer and an animator. It seems you have a music (and sound) guy, that's nice.<br /> <br /> <b>Project Manager</b><br /> Ideally there should be a project manager. He decides the direction of project, create continuous detailed step-by-step progressions and whip everyone's butts to keep on track. Basically he's who everyone hates but needs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most hobbyist programmers lack the experience and skills to collaborate (and play nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) with others.<br /> <br /> <b>Programming</b><br /> It makes or breaks the project. Decide fast on platform, technology, testing methods and stick to them!<br /> <br /> Platform: Windows (XP+, 7+, 10+ so on), Macos, Linux, Xbox, Playstation, Andorid, Windows Mobile so on. The most widespread is of course Windows (version XP is no longer supported, 7 and above has the most share, 10 is up and coming but not too widespread yet). I recommend Windows 7 and above.<br /> <br /> Technology: simplest explanations is 2D or 3D. For a new team with minimum experience, go 2D. It simplifies a lot and still looks good. As a bonus, it has much lower system requirements which translate as wider audience.<br /> <br /> <b>How much is the budget? When is the deadline?</b> If you have money, to safe time and lots of pains, license some ready made engines. If minimum budget then the programmer needs to build some new engines from scratch. Which means lots of time, lots of bugs, lots of headache. If you have a programmer who is proficient in C++, then you're in luck. C# is okay for simple hobbyist projects and Java has sub par performance. Forget about other languages.<br /> <br /> <b>Animation</b><br /> Unless you're creating a text only game or have static graphics, you need an animator to create dynamic graphic (thus, more lifelike). How amazing do you want the graphic? Depends on the programming.<br /> <br /> <b>Audio</b><br /> Same as visual, depends on programming. Avoid voice/speech for first project. It requires more time and equipment, harder to change the lines, more i18n l10n works.<br /> <br /> <b>Testing / QA</b><br /> Most newcomers neglect this. But you really need a good QA. Can't stress this enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Documentation</b><br /> Prevent headache later on by paying attention on this from the very beginning. Maintain a good docs.<br /> <br /> WoD is a very complicated game. Thinking of translating just the core manual alone into code gives me a headache. So start small. Don't refer to professional games, especially those made by highly funded studios. Look at independent games made by small team.<br /> <br /> Maybe build a 10-hour RPG with a linear story with a few NPCs and one fixed PC. Trust me, even 10-hour gameplay is a lot of work for an RPG! (I'm talking about a good story-based RPG here not a button mashing action &quot;RPG&quot;.).<br /> <br /> If you do start this project, <b>persevere</b>! A project is always the most fun before it begins. It goes downhill fast and only becomes worse and worse. The grueling hard work, expenses, emotional distress, real life distractions, unreached expectations can all be too much too soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with you except one thing: looking at big budget games. Inspiration could be found everywhere and money doesn't change a thing. I saw many big budget games that were failures in my eye for example (sorry hard core fans) Vampire the Masquerade Redemption and some independent games which were great (New Star Soccer is my favourite one). And I don't think that if WoD is a role playing game then video games based on it should be RPGs tok. My players have a lot of fun using video games as feelies during my games sometimes. They won some money betting matches simulated in Football Manager series or leading soldiers to battle in 101 Airborne in Normandy. One even drove a truck in Euro Trucker <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 12-04-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar"